{
  "_comment": [
    "Enumerated request-shape typing debt, checked by `pnpm check:request-shapes`.",
    "Every entry is a field the guard WOULD flag, kept with a reason rather than typed today.",
    "An entry that matches nothing FAILS the check \u2014 pay the debt, delete the line.",
    "Adding an entry is a deliberate act: prefer typing the field.",
    "`methodParams` enumerates the engine-method parameter keys (`method.key`) still typed bare any, each with a code from `methodParamReasons`. It may only shrink: a typed key that regresses is not on it and fails."
  ],
  "allow": {
    "GetDrawDataArgs.status": "Genuinely OPEN by design \u2014 a publish-state channel key, PUBLIC unless a provider uses a private one. The guard's registry infers from the field NAME, and `status` is polysemous across the domain (Person.status is a bare string, PracticeRegistration.status is PracticeRegistrationStatusUnion); the union it suggests here is the wrong one. This entry records a deliberate non-fix, not deferred work.",
    "GetEventDataArgs.status": "The same publish-state channel key as GetDrawDataArgs.status, and the same deliberate non-fix.",
    "PublishEventArgs.status": "The same publish-state channel key as GetDrawDataArgs.status, and the same deliberate non-fix.",
    "GenerateDrawDefinitionArgs.qualifyingProfiles": "Archaeology, not typing. The shape is assembled across generateEventWithDraw.ts, generateDrawStructuresAndLinks.ts and qualifyingGeneration.ts with roundTarget/structureProfiles nesting that no single site declares. Needs a reading pass before a type can be honest.",
    "ScheduledMatchUpArgs.matchUp": "Called with STORED matchUps from mutate paths (scheduleItems.ts:579,871,956,1023) and with hydrated ones from query paths, and only `.schedule` and `.timeItems` are ever read off it. `MatchUp | HydratedMatchUp` is the likely type but is unverified against every call site. An earlier reason here asserted callers pass 'partially-assembled records mid-hydration'; the call sites do not show that, so it is removed rather than repeated.",
    "TransitionRecordStatusArgs.record": "Deliberately generic \u2014 the function transitions a status on ANY record in ANY collection, keyed by collectionKey/idKey. A narrower type would defeat its purpose.",
    "CallListenerArgs.payloads": "Subscription payloads are topic-shaped and provider-defined; the factory does not constrain what a subscriber receives.",
    "CallListenerArgs.notices": "Deprecated back-compat alias for payloads, slated for removal in a future major. Typing a field on its way out is wasted motion.",
    "HandleCaughtErrorArgs.params": "The arbitrary argument object of whichever engine method threw.",
    "HandleCaughtErrorArgs.err": "A caught value. TypeScript types `catch` bindings as `unknown` or `any` by design and this is that value.",
    "AddCourtsArgs.courtTimings": "Per-court timing overrides, indexed by court ordinal (addCourt.ts:166) and spread into a per-date availability object, so the shape is whatever the caller supplies. `addCourts` is a PUBLIC engine method (factoryEngineMethods.ts, venueGovernor/mutate.ts), so typing it would both invent a contract that was never authored and be a consumer-build break. An earlier reason here claimed the mocks surface was the only producer \u2014 that was wrong, and being public is the stronger argument for authoring the shape deliberately rather than inferring it.",
    "BuildTournamentRecordArgs.eventDataDocs": "Raw provider documents from an external source system. The builder's contract is that it accepts whatever the source emits.",
    "BuildTournamentRecordArgs.matchUpDocs": "Raw provider documents; see eventDataDocs.",
    "BuildTournamentRecordArgs.participantDocs": "Raw provider documents; see eventDataDocs."
  },
  "methodParamReasons": {
    "untyped": "The source function destructures its parameters without a type annotation, so every key is an implicit any. Typing it means writing the Args type from the body; not done yet.",
    "record": "An engine-resolved record key (tournamentRecord, event, drawDefinition, structure) the source function declares any. The record type is known; the call sites, internal and test, have not been checked against it yet.",
    "ladder": "Ladder keys: the ladder tests drive these functions with partial record stubs, so the record types cannot be applied without changing the fixtures.",
    "qualifying": "The qualifying-profile shape is assembled across several generators; see GenerateDrawDefinitionArgs.qualifyingProfiles.",
    "validator": "A validator receives what it checks; its input is better typed unknown than guessed, and that is a separate pass.",
    "pending": "Declared any and not yet typed: the value shape has to be read from the body and its callers."
  },
